fits  outweigh the potential risks for kids  flags are also flying at half mast  all over the Commonwealth this is the  Canadian warship hmcs Margaret Brook  deployed in the Arctic  we're back from London in a moment  welcome back to London the queen met a  multitude of people over her 70-year  Reign and we're hearing lots of funny  and touching memories from those people  she traveled to Canada more than any  other country Mike drolet looks back at  some of the memorable moments from her  many trips there and here's from  Canadians who were left with a lasting  impression of the late monarch  There are rules when you meet a monarch  no matter the event or occasion  Canadians are planning to meet Queen  Elizabeth all should have received an  education on proper etiquette  so bewildered was NHL player Mike Ricci  as the queen was set to drop the  ceremonial Puck at a 2002 game in  Vancouver he did his best to class  things up tucking his long hair into his  sweater putting in his fake teeth and  then kept mostly quiet  all across Canada the Queen's passing is  being honored in traditional ways bells  ringing in Banff flowers around Queen's  Park and Toronto books of condolence for  people to sign in Edmonton Ottawa and  other cities but those who had the  privilege of meeting or say the same  thing all the formality and nervousness  that came with standing before the crown  melted upon meeting the person wearing  it Maggie Archibald experienced it  firsthand when she and her twin sister  were chosen to meet the queen at a  Buckingham Palace garden party last the  time she was 93 years old and she knows  she was smiling she was you know engaged  you know she was witty and when the  royal family visited Brian Bailey's  Manitoba Family Farm in 1970 they saw a  global icon who was firmly grounded you  know people think her as being Regal and  you know wearing crowns and so on here  she was just so ordinary she took  pictures went for a horseback ride and  relaxed in a la